{"base":"96251f128e2d0f5f58f05d5064672b37474ef409","description":"Move release lookup methods to library\n\nRead commands (show, fetch) were failing with \"no release found\"\nwhen the release was created by a non-delegate, because all\nlookups were delegate-scoped. Reads don't modify anything so\nthere's no squatting risk — split into unscoped reads and\ndelegate-scoped writes.\n\n- Add find_unique_by_oid and find_delegate_release to Releases\n- Add error::FindRelease as the canonical lookup error type\n- Use unscoped find_unique_by_oid for read commands (show, fetch)\n- Use delegate-scoped find_delegate_release for write commands\n- Move delegate filtering tests from binary to library\n- Remove binary wrapper functions, call library methods directly\n\n\nFix failure to export after successful fetch\n\n- FsStore::export_path_impl rejects relative paths with\n  an IO error; default output_path is relative (name_cid)\n- Convert to absolute dest/dest_dir via std::path::absolute before\n  creating the runtime, covering both blob and collection cases","oid":"5eb4fc5aaf78b2ed115ba60a7e24097454b19b94","type":"revision"}